Resource loading
----------------------

Heavyweight resource objects are retrieved by calling the `get()` method of **ResourceItem**.
If the resource was already loaded it is retrieved from cache; otherwise it is loaded and stored weakly.
When the system is low on memory, resources not retained by a Component or a **Scene** node become eligible for garbage collection.

```java
// Declarative — preferred for static assets
ColorItem accent = Resources.create(new WebColor("0088D3"));
Color c = accent.get();

// Dynamic — anonymous ResourceItem, still cached by path
Image dynamic = Resources.create(new RelImage(item.getImagePath())).get();
```

ResourceItem
-----------------

There are 3 ways to declare resources, each one is available for all kind of resources with special feature for parameters.

* [With Resources.create(ResourceParam)](#create)
* [With Enumeration allowing customization](#enum)
* [Dynamically](#dynamic)


<a name="create"></a>
### With Resources.create(ResourceParam)
	
The first way is to hold static field declaration instantiated  with custom 'factory' Resources (not named, with an overloaded create method to avoid later cast).
This static fields can be hold in any class you want but we recommend to store them into an **Interface** used 'as' an enum.
It's better to have an interface per resource type to avoid big file that blends all resources.
Another interesting trick, is to add a static import on related static Resource.create method to shorten the resource declaration (Ctrl+Shift+M with Eclipse).
	
Static import declaration:

```java

import static org.jrebirth.af.core.resource.Resources.create;
```

Example of Web color declaration:

```java

    ColorItem TEST_COLOR_WEB_1 = create(new WebColor("0088D3"));
```

<a name="enum"></a>
### With Enumeration

The other way to declare is a little bit complex, it implies to create an _enum_ that implements a **ResourceItem** interface.
But it requires to add use a custom syntax to use default method.


```java
public enum EnumColors implements ColorEnum {

    // @formatter:off

    /** Color for slide title, white. */
    SLIDE_TITLE {{ web("FFFFFF", 1.0); }},

    /** Color for blue shape, xxx. */
    SHAPE_BLUE{{ web("3495CE", 1.0); }},

    /** Color for drop shadow, black. */
    DROP_SHADOW{{ web("000000", 0.8); }},

    /** Color for inner shadow, white. */
    INNER_SHADOW{{ web("FFFFFE", 0.3); }};

}
```

Severals default methods exist, at least one per **ResourceParams** to create.


<a name="dynamic"></a>
### Dynamically

We can load dynamicalli resource by creating "anonymous" **ResourceItem**, the resource will be kept within cache if memory is not constrained otherwise it will be deleted.
Another call with the same path will hit the cache and the image will be only stored once, but created as many times as deleted and retrieved again.


```java
            final Image image = Resources.create(new RelImage(item.getImage())).get();
```

In this sample _item.getImage()_ return the relative srtring path of the image.


### With @Preload

Resource enums annotated with `@Preload` are automatically loaded during application startup (in the preInit phase). This is useful for fonts that CSS references — they must be available before stylesheets are applied.


```java
@Target(ElementType.TYPE)
@Retention(RetentionPolicy.RUNTIME)
@Inherited
@Documented
public @interface Preload {

}
```


Samples
----------------

### Color

For example to manage web color, (basic hexadecimal string #00CC00), you have to use this declaration:

```java

    ColorItem TEST_COLOR_WEB_1 = create(new WebColor("0088D3"));
```


### Font

For example to manage the **Turtles** font, you have to use this declaration:

```java

    FontItem TEST_REAL_FONT_1 = create(new RealFont(TestFontNames.Turtles, 10.0));
```

Hereafter the enumeration that stores font names.


```java
public enum TestFontNames implements FontName {

    /** Turtles. */
    Turtles,

    /** Report 1942. */
    Report_1942,
}
```


### StyleSheet

Stylesheets are declared as `StyleSheetItem` and loaded via `addCSS()`:


```java
public interface SampleStyles {

    /** The application main style sheet. */
    StyleSheetItem MAIN = create(new StyleSheet("sample"));

}
```

Apply to the scene from your Application class:

```java
@Override
protected void preInit() {
    addCSS(getScene(), SampleStyles.MAIN);
}
```

Or apply locally from a View:

```java
@Override
protected void initView() {
    addCSS(SampleStyles.LOCAL);
}
```

### Image ###

```java
import static org.jrebirth.af.core.resource.Resources.create;

ImageItem BANNER = create(new RelImage("images/banner.png"));

// Usage:
Image img = BANNER.get();
myImageView.setImage(img);
```

Relative paths resolve from the declaring class's package on the classpath.


### AudioClip &amp; Media

These resource types (`AudioClipItem`, `MediaItem`) are defined in the JRebirth API but not yet implemented in core. They are planned for a future release and will follow the same ResourceItem/ResourceParam pattern as other resources.

